          "step_id": "tile_pandas_dataframe_reading.s06",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "pandas.reading_data"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Reading Data",
          "title": "Loading CSV and Excel files into a DataFrame",
          "lede": "Delivery records often arrive as CSV exports or Excel workbooks. Two pandas functions cover both.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_pandas_dataframe_reading.s06.b1",
              "role": "intro",
              "text": "Before pandas can work with your delivery records, you read the file into a DataFrame. `pd.read_csv(\"orders.csv\")` is the main function for reading a delimited text file — such as a CSV — into a DataFrame. `pd.read_excel(\"orders.xlsx\", sheet_name=\"January\")` reads an Excel workbook instead.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "pandas.reading_data"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "pandas.reading_data#tb1",
                  "pandas.reading_data#tb2",
                  "pandas.reading_data#tb3"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "pandas.reading_data#f1",
                  "pandas.reading_data#f2"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_pandas_dataframe_reading.s06.b2",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "`read_csv()` takes the file path (or URL) as its first argument. `read_excel()` additionally takes `sheet_name` to choose which sheet to load — that is why the Excel call names `\"January\"` but the CSV call does not need to. `read_csv()` also accepts `sep` to change the field delimiter: `pd.read_csv(\"orders.csv\", sep=\";\")` handles a semicolon-delimited export correctly.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "pandas.reading_data"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "pandas.reading_data#tb4",
                  "pandas.reading_data#tb5"
