              "role": "mechanism",
              "text": "`read_csv()` takes the file path (or URL) as its first argument. `read_excel()` additionally takes `sheet_name` to choose which sheet to load — that is why `pd.read_excel(\"orders.xlsx\", sheet_name=\"January\")` names the sheet but `pd.read_csv(\"orders.csv\")` does not need to. `read_csv()` also accepts `sep` to change the delimiter: `pd.read_csv(\"orders.csv\", sep=\";\")` handles a semicolon-delimited export.",
